# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Achernar Web Frontend — environment template
# Copy to `.env` (local, git-ignored) or `.env.development` (committed dev
# defaults) and adjust as needed. Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Daemon (local edge control). Used when the hardware transport is "daemon"
# (i.e. running inside the Tauri desktop app, talking to the local daemon).
VITE_DAEMON_URL=http://localhost:3030/api/v1
VITE_DAEMON_WS=ws://localhost:3030/ws/telemetry

# Cloud backend (Django). Used when the hardware transport is "django"
# (i.e. running in a normal browser, reaching hardware via the cloud relay).
VITE_CLOUD_API=http://localhost:8000/api

# Hardware transport override: "daemon" | "django".
# Leave UNSET to auto-detect: the Tauri desktop runtime resolves to "daemon",
# a plain browser resolves to "django" (see src/lib/runtime.ts). Set this only
# to force a transport, e.g. to test the Django relay path from a browser while
# a local daemon is also running.
# VITE_HARDWARE_TRANSPORT=django
